    "engineering_justification": "Classes CS (surface scratch), CFO (conductive debris), and BMFO (laminate particulate) represent non-geometric surface anomalies. In accordance with IPC-A-600 Section 3, scratches do not violate functional integrity unless reducing conductor thickness by >10% or bridging spacing. To prevent detector confusion on conductive copper boundaries, the 6 core functional defect modes (open, short, mouse bite, spur, copper splash, missing pad) are prioritized for edge detection, while foreign objects are flagged via the Reference Comparison diff-pipeline."
